WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.147
Retrieval is not simply a question of finding relevant chunks.

00:00:04.147 --> 00:00:08.232
We also have to decide how much evidence to send forward.

00:00:08.232 --> 00:00:11.702
Top-k controls the number of retrieved chunks.

00:00:11.702 --> 00:00:18.547
A larger value may capture more evidence, but it can also add noise and increase prompt length.

00:00:18.547 --> 00:00:25.757
A similarity threshold can remove weak matches, but the threshold should be evaluated on your own data.

00:00:25.757 --> 00:00:30.019
Score ranges can change across embedding models and search systems.

00:00:30.628 --> 00:00:35.910
The context budget controls the total amount of retrieved text placed into the prompt.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.545
These settings interact with each other.

00:00:38.545 --> 00:00:44.750
For a short knowledge base, top three or top five may be reasonable starting points.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:49.320
For longer technical documents, you may need a different strategy.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.950
Do not optimize these values by intuition alone.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:56.184
Use an evaluation set and compare results.
